Modifications
Datajack: Datajacks are cybertechnology implants that allow metahumans to directly access computers and information with their mind. They typically resemble a coin-sized dataport that is implanted either on the side of the head (typically in the temporal region of the skull, behind the ear or on the temple) or the back of the neck (just below the brainstem).

Control Rig (3): This implant harnesses the raw data-coordinating and synchronization power of the middle brain for the express purpose of directly manipulating vehicles and drones (and other devices like turrets).

Attention Coprocessor (3): A cybernetic implant in the frontal cortex and limbic system improves continuous partial attention, helping to keep track of events in the background without losing the foreground. Also improves the sensory cortex to help you glean as much as possible from incoming sensory data.

Smartlink: An implant that links a smartlinked weapon to the users vision, placing a crosshair wherever the weapon is aiming.

Synaptic Accelerators (3): Nanotech that supercharges the synaptic connections in your brain, allowing you to process information faster and send impulses throughout your body more effectively.

Reaction Enhancers (Rating 3): Nanotech that augments parts of the spinal column with superconducting materials that can increase physical reaction time.

